    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3af1c80c_6d60d567",
        "filename": "src/cpu/aem_generic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000159
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-11T12:21:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am having internal discussions about the potential cache coherency and related issues. The PSCI code releases the locks after calling this function, that might be problematic. However, C TF-A does the same here: https://github.com/ARM-software/arm-trusted-firmware/blob/1ba0d3306e7ecdbd1c8e6e18f6d6d618f8bd3060/lib/psci/psci_off.c#L119\nIt calls the power down functions in line 119, then releases the locks in line 143.\nI will address these issues in a separate patch if needed.",
      "parentUuid": "c1e89c5b_7830a42d",
      "revId": "a0837208ea66b941fb162f1fdf91482546961d02",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e53850c1_a08df6e3",
        "filename": "src/cpu/aem_generic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000309
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-27T13:02:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If there are requirements on when `power_down_level0` can be called to avoid undefined behaviour then it should be an unsafe function.",
      "parentUuid": "3af1c80c_6d60d567",
      "revId": "a0837208ea66b941fb162f1fdf91482546961d02",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9622c0d3_83fd2bef",
        "filename": "src/cpu/aem_generic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000159
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-27T14:58:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIK, this is safe, because it flushes the caches and the platform supports hardware-assisted coherency. C TF-A only requires extra steps (i.e. invalidating certain memory ranges) when the platform does support HW coherency.\nWe decided at the beginning that RF-A only supports platforms with HW coherency.\nFor future platform we will see whether they restrict this function to be only called at a known step of the power down sequence.",
      "parentUuid": "e53850c1_a08df6e3",
      "revId": "a0837208ea66b941fb162f1fdf91482546961d02",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
